content:
{
  "asset": "P-108 — AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-23110, raw-water transfer line",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Shaft-seal leakage is approximately one drop every two seconds, equivalent to 30 drops/minute. The evidence provides no numerical allowable seal-leakage rate or leak-based shutdown threshold, so a numerical pass/fail comparison cannot be made. The applicable manual troubleshooting entry treats leakage at the shaft seal as a defect requiring mechanical-seal replacement and an alignment check.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration is 3.2 mm/s. Under the HF-300 Figure 3 criterion for vibration velocity in mm/s RMS measured on bearing housings, this is above the 2.8 mm/s Zone A/B boundary and below the 4.5 mm/s Zone B/C boundary, placing it provisionally in Zone B, 'Long-term operation.' It is below the 7.1 mm/s boundary for Zone D, the highest severity zone, so this reading does not trigger the site immediate-stop rule. The classification is provisional because the report does not confirm RMS measurement, measurement location, or that this is the highest reading from both housings as required by the condition-monitoring procedure.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing-housing temperature is 68°C. The applicable HF-300 housing-surface limits are normal up to 70°C, alarm at 80°C, and trip at 90°C. Thus 68°C is 2°C below the upper normal value, 12°C below alarm, and 22°C below trip. It is not a documented high bearing temperature, and the site requirement for a priority-1 work order applies only above the manufacturer's alarm limit, so that P1 trigger is not met.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "P2 is assigned for planned correction of the active seal leak. Neither documented emergency criterion is met by the reported values: vibration is not in Zone D and temperature is not above the 80°C alarm or at the 90°C trip. This does not remove the requirement for a controlled shutdown, isolation, and drain before seal work.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Worn or cracked mechanical-seal faces are a primary documented cause. In addition, if component seal HF3-450 is installed, SB-2026-014 identifies early failure of that seal on this pump's serial range, caused by a revised sleeve tolerance.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The seal may have run dry. This is a documented cause of seal leakage; the HF-300 has Plan 11 flush from pump discharge and must never be run dry. No dry-running event or flush-condition evidence is included in the report.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment is another documented cause of seal leakage and could also contribute to vibration. No alignment measurements are supplied.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing wear, impeller imbalance or damage, and cavitation remain inspection-only possibilities for the vibration finding; none is confirmed. The 3.2 mm/s value is Zone B rather than the restricted or damage-likely zones, and the 68°C temperature does not by itself establish bearing wear.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before shutdown, confirm that the reported vibration is velocity in mm/s RMS on a bearing housing, measure both bearing housings, and classify the highest reading with Figure 3. Check NPSH as part of the documented vibration/cavitation investigation. If the highest reading falls in the manufacturer's highest severity zone, stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C09",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump for mechanical-seal replacement. Apply the electrical, mechanical-isolation, line-break, drain, and vent controls listed under safety_controls before opening the pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the 68 kg back pull-out assembly using the required lifting arrangements, then remove the impeller nut and impeller and withdraw the seal and sleeve.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Record the installed seal type and inspect the seal and sleeve. Inspect the sleeve specifically for scoring and replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. Verify the Plan 11 flush arrangement from pump discharge and investigate any evidence of dry running; never run the pump dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Inspect the bearings and impeller for the possible vibration causes. Do not automatically replace bearings on the current readings: replace both bearings as a pair only if either shows wear, noise, or high temperature. The reported 68°C housing temperature is within the manual's normal range.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit one new HF3-450B cartridge mechanical seal; do not fit HF3-450 on this serial-number pump. HF3-450B is pre-set, so no sleeve measurement is needed for seal setting. Fit a new HF3-120 casing gasket in accordance with the seal-replacement procedure.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reassemble and tighten disturbed fasteners using lightly oiled threads: M16 casing bolts to 210 Nm, M24 impeller nut to 160 Nm, and M12 bearing-housing bolts to 85 Nm if disturbed. Tighten the HF3-450B seal gland nuts to 30 Nm; do not use the manual's superseded 25 Nm value for this asset.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check shaft alignment as required for seal-leak troubleshooting. Use a laser alignment tool after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing. Apply tolerances of 0.05 mm parallel offset and 0.05 mm per 100 mm angular alignment.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Cartridge mechanical seal, quantity one; required replacement for HF3-450 on HF-300 serial HF3-22000 and above. Pre-set, with 30 Nm gland-nut torque.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket, quantity one; fit new during seal replacement and whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve, quantity one conditional on inspection; install only if existing sleeve scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3, quantity one conditional on inspection; if bearing replacement is justified, replace it together with HF3-510 as a pair.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3, quantity one conditional on inspection; if either bearing shows wear, noise, or high temperature, replace it together with HF3-512 as a pair.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "For work inside the pump or on its seal, apply electrical isolation and lock-out/tag-out at the MCC; mechanically isolate both suction and discharge valves; and obtain a line-break permit, draining and venting before line break.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg, exceeding the 25 kg lifting-control threshold. Use a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the raw-water line is confirmed to be chemically dosed, provide chemical goggles and nitrile gloves for the work.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If condition monitoring identifies vibration in the manufacturer's highest severity zone, stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart. The reported 3.2 mm/s value alone does not activate this control.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical-seal replacement standard labour: 4.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser-alignment standard labour: 1.5 hours with 1 technician; include for the alignment check planned in this work order.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional bearing-replacement labour: add the standard 6.0 hours with 2 technicians only if inspection establishes that either bearing requires replacement and the pair must be changed. It is not automatically included on the basis of the current normal temperature and Zone B vibration.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal-part conflict: the manual parts table lists component seal HF3-450, while SB-2026-014 prohibits fitting HF3-450 and requires cartridge seal HF3-450B on affected pumps. The bulletin was issued 14 March 2026 and applies to HF-300 serial HF3-22000 and above. P-108 is serial HF3-23110 and therefore is within range, so HF3-450B governs for this asset.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal-gland torque conflict: manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts, whereas SB-2026-014 gives 30 Nm for HF3-450B. Because P-108's HF3-23110 serial number is within the bulletin's HF3-22000-and-above range, use 30 Nm for this repair. The other Table 5 torque values remain applicable to disturbed fasteners.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "What is the allowable shaft-seal leakage rate, the leak-based operating or shutdown restriction, and the post-repair leakage acceptance criterion? The supplied manual identifies leakage and its corrective action but gives no numerical leakage limit. [C09, C10]",
    "Is the reported 3.2 mm/s an RMS velocity measured on a bearing housing, which housing was measured, and what is the reading on the other housing? The procedure requires both housings to be measured and the highest reading classified. [C06, C07]",
    "Which seal is currently installed, is there any history of dry running, and is the Plan 11 flush from pump discharge healthy? These facts are needed to distinguish the documented seal-failure causes but are not in the report. [C02, C09, C13]",
    "What are the sleeve scoring depth, shaft-alignment readings, bearing condition, impeller condition, and NPSH results? These determine whether the conditional sleeve, bearing-pair, or additional corrective work is required. [C09, C10, C13]",
    "Is the raw-water transfer line chemically dosed? If it is, chemical goggles and nitrile gloves are mandatory; the service description alone does not establish whether this control applies. [C15]",
    "Table 6 provides standard times for seal replacement, bearing replacement, and laser alignment but no separate allowance for NPSH investigation, additional diagnostics, or commissioning. Confirm the required schedule allowance for any such added work. [C09, C12]"
  ]
}
